      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the body say what fails without this patch? As far as I can see, the pin ranges don\u0027t change units with the caller today: they are in kernel pages for every caller, so a 4KB process gets `-EINVAL` from `ASHMEM_PIN` and `ASHMEM_UNPIN` for ranges that are 4KB- but not 16KB-aligned (a whole-region pin with `len \u003d\u003d 0` works).\n\nThe message also doesn\u0027t mention the `ASHMEM_GET_PIN_STATUS` change, and if the LRU fix goes (see `free_lru()`), \"update LRU accounting\" can go too. The last paragraph describes how the Rust helpers are written; could it say why they are needed instead?",
