      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:34:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this change needed? As far as I can see, nothing fails without it: with `__page_align()` a 4KB process can map up to the 16KB-rounded size, as a native process can, and the extra 4KB pages lie in the same shmem page, so nothing beyond what a native process can map is exposed. The change only turns those mappings into `-EINVAL`, as on a 4KB kernel.\n\nIf that difference doesn\u0027t matter, would it be OK to drop it? `uapi_page_align()` would then have no user.\n\n`__page_align()` is also needed for x86_64 16K emulation.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "9e095111b23b99fe6f7fd2866c5b9ff2c5a17189",
