      "message": "It looks like this fixes a bug that isn\u0027t specific to P3S: `ASHMEM_GET_PIN_STATUS` is `_IO()`, so `_IOC_SIZE(cmd)` is 0 and `reader.read()` returns `-EFAULT` for every process, native ones included (C ashmem always copied `sizeof(struct ashmem_pin)`). android17-6.18 and android-mainline still have the bug.\n\nWould you mind sending this as its own `ANDROID: ashmem:` patch to android-mainline, so that every ACK branch gets it? `pin_unpin()` could then keep taking a plain `UserSliceReader`: every caller passes `Some(...)`, so the `(0, 0)` branch is unreachable.\n\nThe `ASHMEM_GET_FILE_ID` arm above only changes formatting (to a 115-column line), so could it stay as it is?",
