      "message": "I\u0027m worried `uapi_page_size()` changes this count on x86_64 with 16KB page size emulation: there it follows `__page_shift()` (14 with `page_shift\u003d14`), while `mm_pte_shift()` and the range pages stay at 4KB, so `ASHMEM_PURGE_ALL_CACHES` would return about a quarter of today\u0027s count.\n\nCould this use `mm.page_size()`, as `pin_unpin()` does with `mm.page_mask()`? Native arm64 processes would still get 16KB pages and 4KB processes 4KB pages, and `uapi_page_size()` would have no user.",
