      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:34:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the test focus on what this patch changes? As far as I can see, the default-alignment and hint checks, the 4KB-offset mapping and coherency checks and the native 4KB-offset `mmap()` check all pass without this patch: they cover the generic P3S mmap paths rather than ashmem.\n\nThe `--purge-*` modes also never run, since `compat_checks()` doesn\u0027t call them; they need `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` and purge every unpinned ashmem region on the system. Could they either run from `compat_checks()` (skipping without `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`) or go? Keeping the pin, unpin and status checks in both kinds of process and on the shared fd would make the test much smaller than 447 lines.",
