      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:34:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this doesn\u0027t skip on kernels without P3S. On a 4KB kernel (arm64 or x86_64), `personality()` accepts `ADDR_4KB_COMPAT_PAGE_SIZE` and keeps it across `execv()`, so after `exec_compat()`, `p3s_require_compat()` passes and the 16KB alignment and native checks fail. And if the re-exec fails, `exec_compat()` reports a failure rather than a skip.\n\n`p3s_compat_main()` already handles both (`__aarch64__`, `getpagesize() !\u003d NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE`, and `EINVAL`/`EPERM` from the re-exec). Would it work to keep the `p3s_run_mode()` dispatch for the child roles and end `main()` with:\n\n```\n\treturn p3s_compat_main(argc, argv, compat_checks);\n```\n\nThis patch then wouldn\u0027t need `exec_compat()` and `p3s_vexec_or_die()` in kselftest_p3s.h, nor the double blank line before them.",
